messages:
anya: heads-up: found a reproducible goroutine leak in the go sample app when cancelling a long-running generator stream (SIGINT). looks like token refresh blocks and never observes ctx.Done().

matt: ouch. snippet?

anya: small repro: 
```go
func stream(ctx context.Context) {
  for {
    _, err := client.Generate(ctx, req) // streaming responses
    if err != nil {
      return
    }
  }
}

func main() {
  ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
  go func() {
    sig := make(chan os.Signal, 1)
    signal.Notify(sig, os.Interrupt)
    <-sig
    cancel()
  }()
  go refresher(ctx) // background auth refresh
  stream(ctx)
}

func refresher(ctx context.Context) {
  for {
    t := blockingGetToken() // internal call not using ctx
    select {
    case <-time.After(30 * time.Second): _ = t
    case <-ctx.Done(): return
    }
  }
}
```

anya: after ctrl-c, stream returns but process stays alive. pprof shows goroutine stuck in blockingGetToken.

sam: classic: TokenSource/refresh path isn't cancellable. app-level cancel doesn't help.

jenna: agreed. two practical paths: (1) update sample app to use signal.NotifyContext and wrap blocking calls, (2) add ctx-aware refresh in the SDK. We've discussed adding Refresh(ctx) on TokenSource and keeping Refresh() for compatibility.

matt: short-term patch: change sampleapp to use an http.Client that accepts ctx for refresh requests, or wrap blockingGetToken with a select that aborts on ctx using a helper wrapper. long-term: implement NewContextAwareTokenSource in the SDK to adapt old token sources.

anya: i'll open a PR for the sample app + a ticket for the SDK change. will include a unit test that simulates a stalled token server (server accepts connection and delays response) so CI will catch leaks.

ci-bot: Created task RW-4217: "go sdk: context-aware token refresh for long-running streams" and queued e2e run.

jenna: also add a short note in the generator onboarding doc: "Make token refresh cancellable for long-lived streams."

anya: thanks — attaching small pprof and repro in the ticket. will ping when PR is up.
